(* README *)

1 - Summary
    -------

    M001 is a constructive, checker-first proof system for the closed
    implication/falsity language

      A, B ::= Bot | Imp A B

    It provides finite contexts and proof scripts, functional and finite-data
    axiom sources, a total Boolean checker, executable MP/deduction/reductio
    transformations, and a proof that checked derivability agrees with the
    corresponding inductive closure.

    M001 is entirely syntactic. It contains no truth predicate, semantic
    evaluator, model structure, proof search, quotation, self-application, or
    fixed-point principle.


2 - Reading Boundary
    ----------------

    `Formula` has only `Bot` and `Imp`. Object-language negation is the
    abbreviation

      formula_negation A = Imp A Bot.

    `AxiomSet` is a caller-supplied Boolean membership function and need not
    have a finite enumeration. `FiniteAxiomSet` stores a literal formula list
    for applications whose theory description must itself be finite data.

    A `RegulatorTheory` combines a logical profile with an `AxiomSet`.
    Contexts hold temporary assumptions and are not part of the theory.

    A proof is a finite list of formula/justification pairs. Justifications
    are assumptions, available axioms, or MP references into the already
    checked prefix. The central judgement is

      regulator_theory_check_bool R Gamma p A = true.

    It means that every line of `p` checks and the final line is exactly `A`.
    The checker performs validation, not proof search.


3 - Ground-Truth Contract
    ---------------------

    The canonical specification is in the repository-level `contracts.txt`.
    M001 exposes five contracts in dependency order:

      SYNTAX
        No finite formula is syntactically equal to its own negation.

      ADEQUACY
        Checked derivability and inductive derivability coincide.

      DEDUCTION
        The executable deduction transform preserves checking.

      REDUCTIO
        Checked contradiction under A :: Gamma transforms into checked
        object-language negation under Gamma.

      STRUCTURE
        Checked scripts are closed under executable MP composition and remain
        checked under context and regulator-theory enlargement.

      M001_CONTRACT
        The conjunction of the five contracts above.

    `m001_contract_qed` certifies the aggregate. The build checks its generated
    assumption report for undeclared or classical dependencies.


4 - Operational Core
    ----------------

    The retained executable functions are

      regulator_theory_check_bool
      finite_axiom_set_check_bool
      regulator_theory_mp_compose
      regulator_theory_deduction_transform
      regulator_theory_reductio_transform

    Deduction compiles a proof of `B` under `A :: Gamma` into a proof of
    `Imp A B` under `Gamma`. Reductio is deduction specialized to conclusion
    `Bot`; it is constructive negation introduction, not classical reductio or
    double-negation elimination.

    The extraction starts only from these five roots. Rocq automatically
    retains their computational dependencies in

      _appendix/_artifacts/M001_checker.{ml,mli}


5 - Dependency Tree
    ---------------

    Stdlib
     |
    M001_00_Premises           syntax and finite proof data
     |
    M001_01__Kernel            Boolean checker
     |
    M001_02__Abstraction       deduction transform
     |
    M001_03__Falsity           reductio transform
     |
    M001_04__Certificates      certificate and derivability vocabulary
     |
    M001_05__Application       MP composition
     |
    M001_06__Syntactic_Adequacy
     |
    M001_07__Monotonicity      context/theory monotonicity
     |
    M001_08__Regulation        minimal symbolic-regulator vocabulary
     |
    M001_95_API
     |-- M001_97_Artifacts
     `-- M001_98_Sanity


6 - File Guide
    ----------

    M001_00_Premises.v
      Formula syntax, negation, contexts, axiom sources, logical profiles,
      regulator theories, and proof-script grammar.

    M001_01__Kernel.v
      Formula equality and size, context membership, K/S/optional-EFQ
      recognition, proof-line checking, full script checking, and the finite
      axiom-set checker.

    M001_02__Abstraction.v
      Executable deduction and its checker-level correctness theorem. Most of
      this file is the invariant proof for the generated index map and script.

    M001_03__Falsity.v
      The executable reductio specialization and its correctness theorem.

    M001_04__Certificates.v
      A retained proof-certificate subtype, existential checked derivability,
      and the derivability-level deduction lift.

    M001_05__Application.v
      Proof-script shifting, executable MP composition, checked MP closure,
      and one-line assumption/axiom derivability.

    M001_06__Syntactic_Adequacy.v
      The inductive closure and one checked/inductive adequacy theorem.

    M001_07__Monotonicity.v
      Context and regulator-theory monotonicity, both at the concrete-script
      and existential checked-derivability levels.

    M001_08__Regulation.v
      `SymbolicRegulator`, its paper-facing alias `S_λ`, and existential
      Boolean acceptance. These definitions are retained because L002 uses
      them directly.

    M001_95_API.v
      Stable public import and the five canonical contract definitions.

    M001_97_Artifacts.v
      Aggregate certification, assumption report, and OCaml extraction.

    M001_98_Sanity.v
      One small compile-time probe for each retained operation and contract
      family.


7 - Public API
    ----------

    Operational clients import

      From M001 Require Import M001_95_API.

    The stable vocabulary includes

      Formula, Bot, Imp, formula_negation
      Context, ctx_extend
      AxiomSet, FiniteAxiomSet
      RegulatorLogicProfile, RegulatorTheory
      Justification, ProofLine, Proof
      regulator_theory_checked_derivable
      regulator_theory_inductive_derivable
      context_included, regulator_theory_included
      SymbolicRegulator, S_λ, symbolic_regulator_derivable

    The stable proof endpoints are

      formula_not_self_negation
      regulator_theory_syntactic_adequacy_lemma
      regulator_theory_deduction_checked
      regulator_theory_reductio_checked
      regulator_theory_mp_compose_checked_lemma
      regulator_theory_check_bool_context_monotone_lemma
      regulator_theory_check_bool_regulator_theory_monotone_lemma
      m001_contract_qed

    L001 imports only M001's primitive syntax. L002 imports `M001_95_API`
    explicitly for the operational checker and structural results.


8 - Deliberate Exclusions
    ---------------------

    M001 no longer carries evaluation frames, regulator-instruction
    reification, regulated components or worlds, closure/equivalence adapters,
    negative-precomposition restatements, a reductio-certificate hierarchy,
    dedicated minimal-profile wrappers, or diagnostic proof-length helpers.

    These exclusions do not weaken the five contracts or the executable
    checker. They remove alternate presentations of results already expressed
    by the retained checker, transformations, and structural theorems.
